with the last Jedi being released this  week it seemed like a perfect time to  discuss a question that myself and I'm  sure many other Star Wars fans have  asked over the years what exactly does  the color of a lightsaber mean if we  take a look at the Star Wars movies they  never really mention a reference the  different colors of light saber or what  they mean instead they simply serve as a  tool to represent to the audience who  the heroes and villains are if the  lightsabers green or blue then the  character is associated with the Jedi  and therefore a hero of sorts if the  lightsaber is red then they're  associated with the Sith and essentially  a villain during the making of the  original movies there wasn't a whole lot  of thought placed into the color of a  lightsaber the only reason that Luke's  lightsaber changes from blue to green in  the Return of the Jedi is because it was  very difficult to see Luke's original  blue lightsaber against the backdrop of  the blue sky outside of Jabba's palace  [Music]  when we move away from Cannon and the  movie universe and into the extended  universe the different colors of light  sabers are explained and we even have  some new colors introduced that did not  feature in the movies but we first seem  to understand how a lightsaber is  constructed before we delve into the  colors and what they mean in the heart  of every lightsaber lies a Kyber crystal  the crystal allows the user to  concentrate their energy through the  force all Kyber crystals are originally  clear but once they are attuned to their  user they change to a color that best  represents their skills and traits the  crystals are said to be inherently  attuned to the light side and will  attempt to resist any efforts made by  those of the dark side to use them  within a lightsaber the only way it  could be used by a member of the dark  side is by bending it to their will a  certain dominance through the force this  is referred to as making the crystal  bleed and results in the crimson  lightsabers that we associate with the  Sith  the blue lightsaber is undoubtedly the  most common in the Star Wars franchise  it represents a Jedi warrior a guardian  of the peace  Jedi's who wield the blue lightsaber  often use the Force on a more physical  level essentially a jack-of-all-trades  but a master of none the blue lightsaber  is ultimately a sign of a well balanced  Jedi and we see characters such as  obi-wan Kenobi Anakin Skywalker and even  Rey using a blue lightsaber the green  lightsaber is an indication of a Jedi  consular these Jedi had a very strong  connection to the force and they  preferred studying and reflect in its  mysteries they would often use numerous  forms of negotiation before resorting to  use in their lightsaber we see some of  those powerful Jedi in existence using  green lightsabers including qui-gon jinn  Yoda and of course Luke Skywalker  the red lightsaber and the SIF go  hand-in-hand at this point their  lightsabers are essentially corrupted by  the dark side as they were themselves  the red signifies intense emotion and  passion anger and hatred all things  we've come to expect from the Sith this  leads us to the rare and unconventional  colors one of the most notorious being  the purple lightsaber of mace windu  during the filming of the prequels there  was no intention of ever having a purple  lightsaber it was actually the actor  that played mace windu Samuel Jackson  who asked George Lucas if his character  could have a purple lightsaber so he  could stand out now the fans and  numerous authors ran of this idea and  with blue and red making purple it  seemed only fitting that the purple  lightsaber would represent a light side  user who was able to use elements of the  dark side we see the power of the purple  lightsaber when mace windu absorbs  Palpatine's force lightning and  redirects it towards him  with all of that being said it  definitely offers a more interesting  explanation than Samuel Jackson just  wanted a purple lightsaber to stand out  the yellow lightsaber is one that we  most commonly see being used by the Jedi  Temple guards these gods often referred  to as Jedi sentinels these sentinels  believed in a balance between skills in  combat and scholarly pursuits there is  no current explanation in Canon as to  how the yellow lightsabers are made the  white lightsaber is one that we see in  Star Wars rebels when ahsoka tano is  reintroduced the only known way to  create a white lightsaber is when the  bleeding process performed by a Sith is  reversed essentially healing the Kyber  crystal assume in the process involved  and the fact that it is used by ahsoka  tano  we can assume that it represents  Redemption the last lightsaber we'll be  covering today is the black or dark  saber an ancient weapon that was once  used by the Jedi it was eventually  stolen by a group of Mandalorians and as  a result it would be passed down through  their generations for many years we also  see Darth Maul use in the dark saber  during the Clone Wars and the origins  behind the saber are unknown unlike the  rounded lightsaber that we've come to  expect the dark saber much closer  resembles a blade or a sword the best  way to summarize what we've discussed  today is that all lightsabers begin  colorless and their crystals change  color depending on the traits of the  user if you were to choose what color  would your lightsaber be  I hope you guys enjoyed the video I know  it's a little different from the regular  content we cover but I do want to  explore some other fictional universes  that I find interesting as always I've  been your host mythology and fiction  explained
 

